00:14:08,300 --> 00:14:12,800
And he says, excuse me, sir, can you tell my brother to divide the inheritance?

235
00:14:12,800 --> 00:14:15,760
You can see where his mindset is, where his focus is.

236
00:14:15,760 --> 00:14:18,780
He's at church listening to a sermon from the Son of God.

237
00:14:18,780 --> 00:14:23,100
And he's thinking about money, resources.

238
00:14:23,100 --> 00:14:28,240
It would be like one of you in the middle of like, I get to the climactic point of my sermon.

239
00:14:28,240 --> 00:14:30,960
I'm preaching the gospel to people who don't yet know Jesus.

240
00:14:30,960 --> 00:14:35,620
And somebody in the back stands up and says, Ryan, can you tell my wife to cool it on the

241
00:14:35,620 --> 00:14:37,900
Lululemon leggings?

242
00:14:37,900 --> 00:14:40,400
Right?

243
00:14:40,400 --> 00:14:43,200
It's like, what are we doing here?

244
00:14:43,200 --> 00:14:44,320
We're doing something.

245
00:14:44,320 --> 00:14:47,100
We're talking about something far greater than this reality.

246
00:14:47,100 --> 00:14:52,500
And the question that this guy has, I use the Lululemon illustration because the question

247
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:54,700
that this guy has comes from a place of privilege.

248
00:14:54,700 --> 00:15:02,340
The fact that his father was a landowner makes him like already far wealthier than like a majority

249
00:15:02,340 --> 00:15:04,600
of the crowd that Jesus is talking to.

250
00:15:04,600 --> 00:15:09,360
Jesus himself being a poor, like homeless, itinerant preacher.

251
00:15:09,360 --> 00:15:13,840
And this guy who's probably one of the richer guys in the crowd is like, hey, let's talk about

252
00:15:13,840 --> 00:15:14,480
my problem.

253
00:15:14,480 --> 00:15:17,940
Well, my brother has my stuff and I want to get it back.

254
00:15:17,940 --> 00:15:23,000
And I think the reality is there's probably some, there's probably some injustice there.

255
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:26,300
Like the brother's probably keeping some things that are rightfully his.

256
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:28,360
And he knows that Jesus is about justice.

257
00:15:28,360 --> 00:15:29,660
So he's like, this is my opportunity.

258
00:15:29,660 --> 00:15:30,780
I got one shot, right?

259
00:15:30,780 --> 00:15:32,960
This guy's going to, he's going to make it right.

260
00:15:32,960 --> 00:15:37,740
But I think this is one of the reasons that Jesus doesn't get lost in the specifics of the

261
00:15:37,740 --> 00:15:40,400
situation because he knows it's already from a place of privilege.

262
00:15:40,400 --> 00:15:46,000
And so what he does instead of dealing with the situations, he launches into teaching on greed.

263
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:53,100
Because the brother is valuing the accumulation of more stuff above his relationship with his brother.

264
00:15:53,100 --> 00:15:56,940
And Jesus wants to expose what's happening in our hearts.

265
00:15:57,540 --> 00:16:00,660
And what this shows about how we view the world.

266
00:16:00,660 --> 00:16:10,100
Christ's main point that he states from the very beginning is be careful not to become greedy because life does not consist in the accumulation of things.

267
00:16:10,200 --> 00:16:15,620
I heard one pastor say it this way this week, having a lot does not mean that you have a life.

268
00:16:15,620 --> 00:16:21,920
And so this is where Jesus is saying, hey, like, it's not a totally ignoring your situation.

269
00:16:21,920 --> 00:16:23,360
He's just saying, this is revealing.

270
00:16:23,360 --> 00:16:26,900
I want to show you what this says about what's true in your heart.

271
00:16:26,900 --> 00:16:32,900
And he goes on in classic Jesus fashion to tell an awesome story that's going to really make his point.

272
00:16:32,900 --> 00:16:37,520
In verse 16, he says, and he told them a parable saying, the land of a rich man.

273
00:16:37,520 --> 00:16:39,760
Everybody say rich man.

274
00:16:40,200 --> 00:16:43,360
The land of a rich man produced plentiful.

275
00:16:43,360 --> 00:16:46,360
And he thought to himself, what shall I do?

276
00:16:46,360 --> 00:16:48,220
For I have nowhere to store my crops.

277
00:16:48,220 --> 00:16:49,920
And he said, I will do this.

278
00:16:49,920 --> 00:16:52,040
I'll tear down my barns and I'll build larger ones.

279
00:16:52,040 --> 00:16:54,120
And then I'll store all my grain and my goods.

280
00:16:54,120 --> 00:16:58,540
And I will say to my soul, love that he's having an internal dialogue with his soul.

281
00:16:58,540 --> 00:17:02,320
Soul, you have ample goods laid up for many years.

282
00:17:02,320 --> 00:17:04,380
Relax, eat, drink, and be merry.

283
00:17:04,380 --> 00:17:10,160
But God said to him, fool, this night, your soul.

284
00:17:10,200 --> 00:17:11,080
Those are required of you.

285
00:17:11,080 --> 00:17:14,680
And the things you have prepared, whose will they be?

286
00:17:14,680 --> 00:17:22,380
So this is the one who lays up a treasure for himself and is not rich towards God.

287
00:17:22,380 --> 00:17:27,080
So Jesus tells the story of a man who's already rich,

288
00:17:27,760 --> 00:17:34,060
trying to decide what he's going to do with the additional resources that his land has produced for him.

289
00:17:34,060 --> 00:17:36,940
And we say his land has produced for him.

290
00:17:36,940 --> 00:17:44,600
But if we know the economic system of the world, we actually know that it's like day workers and tenant farmers who are barely feeding themselves and their family,

291
00:17:44,600 --> 00:17:47,180
who are the ones who gathered this crop for this rich man.

292
00:17:47,540 --> 00:17:50,600
And they are mostly the people that are filling the audience of Jesus.

293
00:17:50,600 --> 00:17:57,680
And so when Jesus begins to tell the story, the people are probably thinking, hey, I know what he can do with the excess grain that he has.

294
00:17:57,680 --> 00:17:58,640
Right?

295
00:17:58,640 --> 00:18:06,700
He can give it to those that the sweat of their brow produced the profit that he is trying to figure out what to do with.

296
00:18:10,760 --> 00:18:20,000
He's surrounded by people in need and the internal dialogue that he's having is what am I going to do with this stuff and how is it going to lead to my security and my joy?

297
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:29,880
And Jesus is exposing this illusion about what life and reality is like by telling this story.

298
00:18:29,880 --> 00:18:35,560
And before you get on your high horse and before I get on my high horse, it's April.

299
00:18:36,760 --> 00:18:42,400
Some of you got some tax return money from the government this past month or two.

300
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:51,720
And I would just ask you to consider to yourself, what did your internal dialogue look like when you got a check that wasn't expected or bigger than it was expected?

301
00:18:51,720 --> 00:18:59,520
What does our internal dialogue say about what we believe about our resources and the world around us?

302
00:19:00,200 --> 00:19:12,520
And the reality is when we read this story and we hear a rich man got more stuff than he needed, every one of us in the room thought about the person one tax bracket above us.

303
00:19:12,520 --> 00:19:24,440
Because all of us, no matter where God has blessed us with, no matter what resource, no matter where we're at in the totem pole, it's always the group above us that needs to hear the message about generosity.

304
00:19:26,660 --> 00:19:29,740
And I myself have struggled with this for a long time.

305
00:19:29,740 --> 00:19:31,020
I was a youth pastor.

306
00:19:31,020 --> 00:19:32,780
My wife was working part-time at a bank.

307
00:19:32,780 --> 00:19:35,580
And we had more than enough.

308
00:19:35,580 --> 00:19:40,220
But I was just, I was looking at the person that now makes what I make.

309
00:19:40,220 --> 00:19:42,660
And I'm like, man, they need to hear a message about generosity.

310
00:19:42,660 --> 00:19:48,500
And now that I'm where I'm at, I'm looking at one step up the ladder.

311
00:19:49,280 --> 00:19:51,160
They need to hear a message about generosity.

312
00:19:51,160 --> 00:19:53,080
And Jesus is just tearing this all down.

313
00:19:53,080 --> 00:19:58,400
He's saying, it's not about how much, it's about the view of the world that you have.

314
00:19:58,400 --> 00:20:01,180
Because conversations about money aren't ultimately about money.

315
00:20:01,180 --> 00:20:04,440
They're about what we love and we put our trust in.

316
00:20:04,440 --> 00:20:08,860
And this man's internal dialogue reveals the way that he views the world.

317
00:20:08,860 --> 00:20:11,300
It is a scarcity mindset.

318
00:20:11,300 --> 00:20:14,700
There is a limited amount of resources and life is short.

319
00:20:14,700 --> 00:20:22,100
So I'm going to store up as much as I can so that I can sit back and relax and have peace and joy.

320
00:20:23,700 --> 00:20:28,060
This is the mindset of the kingdom of this world.

321
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:30,280
Resources are limited and life is short.

322
00:20:30,280 --> 00:20:36,500
And so therefore, it impacts the way that we view the resources around us.

323
00:20:36,500 --> 00:20:42,300
And Jesus makes a clear hyperlink to the story of Ecclesiastes and the Jewish Scriptures.

324
00:20:42,300 --> 00:20:46,700
And if you grew up in the Bible, you know that, or if you grew up in church, you probably know that story.

325
00:20:47,020 --> 00:20:50,600
But for those of you that don't, Solomon wrote the book of Ecclesiastes.

326
00:20:50,600 --> 00:20:55,600
He was one of the most wealthy and successful kings in all of the nation of Israel.

327
00:20:55,600 --> 00:21:03,340
And he launched, just for fun, because he was bored, launched an experiment where he was going to try and find the value of life.

328
00:21:03,340 --> 00:21:06,720
He was going to use all of his resources, all of his wealth, all of his wisdom.

329
00:21:06,720 --> 00:21:09,480
And he was going to figure out where life could be found.

330
00:21:10,100 --> 00:21:21,020
And this eat, drink, and be merry phrase is something that he coined, because what he figured out is no matter what he put his money, his time, his wisdom to, it was all futile and vanity.

331
00:21:21,020 --> 00:21:23,360
It was like striving after the wind.

332
00:21:23,360 --> 00:21:26,960
His conclusion is that life under the sun is vanity.

333
00:21:26,960 --> 00:21:33,700
The illusion of scarcity is the worldview of a life under the sun.

334
00:21:33,700 --> 00:21:38,000
The whole point of the book of Ecclesiastes is there's actually more to life than what's under the sun.

335
00:21:38,460 --> 00:21:50,360
And Jesus is setting this whole worldview up in his parable because he wants us to realize that there is a worldview that we are believing under the sun, that life is short, and that resources are limited.

336
00:21:50,360 --> 00:21:54,780
And therefore, it impacts what we do with them.

337
00:21:54,780 --> 00:22:03,540
Not only that, but life is but a vapor is another thing that Solomon talks about in Ecclesiastes, which gets to the point of the story.

338
00:22:03,620 --> 00:22:09,280
It's like, hey, you think that you have this long future ahead of you, but you never know how long you are going to live.

339
00:22:09,280 --> 00:22:13,560
That should impact the way that we view our resources.

340
00:22:13,560 --> 00:22:20,200
There is a crafty illusion going on under the sun that causes us to think that there are limited resources for a temporary life,

341
00:22:20,200 --> 00:22:25,860
and that true joy and peace is found in accumulating more things, and Jesus is exposing the lie.

342
00:22:26,760 --> 00:22:31,300
And the reality is, in church this morning, most of us are aware that this is a lie.

343
00:22:31,300 --> 00:22:37,000
Most of us would agree with that statement that just because you have a lot, you don't have a life.

344
00:22:37,560 --> 00:22:43,660
But if someone sat down and took a hard look at how you spend your money, at how I spend my money,

345
00:22:43,660 --> 00:22:52,020
would our lives reflect that we believe that reality, or would our finances look more like this under the sun reality?

346
00:22:52,020 --> 00:23:01,500
Jesus says that true life is found in being rich towards God, loving the Lord your God with all of your heart, soul, mind, and strength,

347
00:23:01,500 --> 00:23:03,980
and loving your neighbor as yourself.

348
00:23:03,980 --> 00:23:05,120
Is anybody having fun yet?

349
00:23:05,620 --> 00:23:06,320
Okay, good.

350
00:23:06,320 --> 00:23:11,900
Jesus says that true life is found in loving God and loving others, and over the next few weeks,

351
00:23:11,900 --> 00:23:16,000
I hope that we will double-click just for a couple weeks on our financial decisions

352
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:22,560
and consider what that reveals to us about the worldview that we have.

353
00:23:22,560 --> 00:23:28,000
Are we living with this under-the-sun mentality that leads us to believe the illusion of scarcity?

354
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:31,880
And here's a bonus application.

355
00:23:32,780 --> 00:23:36,600
Sometimes I write things in my notes that's, like, bonus, it's if I have time to get to them.

356
00:23:36,600 --> 00:23:39,880
And usually, even if I don't have time to get to them, I do them anyway.

357
00:23:39,880 --> 00:23:41,780
That's why we're here later than we should be.

358
00:23:41,780 --> 00:23:45,740
So, do you guys want to hear the bonus application, or do you want me to keep going?

359
00:23:45,740 --> 00:23:47,180
Okay.

360
00:23:47,180 --> 00:23:48,200
See, you guys are great.

361
00:23:48,200 --> 00:23:48,900
This is why I do it.

362
00:23:48,900 --> 00:23:50,180
I don't even, I usually don't even tell you.

363
00:23:50,180 --> 00:23:53,200
You guys are getting invited into my internal dialogue.

364
00:23:54,500 --> 00:23:55,020
You're welcome.

365
00:23:55,020 --> 00:24:04,260
So, if you're familiar with the story of Ecclesiastes, you'll know that Solomon even complains about the idea of leaving an inheritance to his kids.

366
00:24:04,260 --> 00:24:11,300
He's, like, super wealthy and wise, and he looks at his kids who are acting a fool, and he's like,

367
00:24:11,300 --> 00:24:14,280
I worked so hard.

368
00:24:14,280 --> 00:24:15,820
I have all this stuff.

369
00:24:16,400 --> 00:24:19,600
And when I die, it's got to go to those knuckleheads.

370
00:24:19,600 --> 00:24:36,000
And when we input that story into this story, I can't help but think, what would the father who worked hard to provide an inheritance for his children be thinking about the fact that his kids are at odds with one another, fighting over the limited resources that he left them?

371
00:24:37,280 --> 00:24:50,340
And that message really hits me hard as a father who feels the pressure to provide for my son, who wants him not to have to worry about food and things like that.

372
00:24:50,340 --> 00:25:03,260
The question for me becomes, would I rather leave Rory a bigger inheritance, or would I rather demonstrate for him the reality that true life is not found in the accumulation of possessions, but in generosity to those around us?

373
00:25:04,820 --> 00:25:19,100
And do I want my son to get a bunch of stuff that he doesn't know how to use in the way that God would want him to use it, or do I want to invite him into the process of using our money the way that God would want us to use it?

374
00:25:19,100 --> 00:25:26,360
And is that leading him to true life, or is me just giving him a pile of stuff at the end of my life leading him to true life?

375
00:25:26,360 --> 00:25:28,340
It'd be a small pile, but it could still be a pile.

376
00:25:28,340 --> 00:25:34,580
And I'm already starting this, and it's an invitation, and it's a process.

377
00:25:34,780 --> 00:25:44,480
He got some money for his birthday, and I told him, I said, buddy, you know, when mommy and daddy get money, we take a little bit aside, and we use it to help others who don't have money.

378
00:25:44,480 --> 00:25:46,000
Is that something that you would like to do?

379
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:47,000
And he said, no.

380
00:25:47,000 --> 00:25:53,220
And I said, okay, we'll get there.

381
00:25:53,220 --> 00:25:53,800
It's all right.

382
00:25:53,800 --> 00:25:55,640
I'm not going to force you to do something.

383
00:25:55,640 --> 00:25:56,580
Like, we'll get there.

384
00:25:56,580 --> 00:25:57,540
We'll figure that out later.

385
00:25:58,060 --> 00:26:02,100
But the question becomes, like, again, it's not a conversation about money.

386
00:26:02,100 --> 00:26:04,040
It's a conversation about our hearts.

387
00:26:04,040 --> 00:26:10,080
And so Jesus directly addresses the greed that comes from this scarcity mindset.

388
00:26:10,080 --> 00:26:12,680
But he doesn't stay on the topic of greed.

389
00:26:12,680 --> 00:26:17,840
He actually moves on to the topic of anxiety in verse 22.

390
00:26:19,180 --> 00:26:26,340
And he said to his disciples, therefore, I tell you, do not be anxious about your life, what you will eat, nor about your body.

391
00:26:26,340 --> 00:26:31,780
What you will put on for life is more than food, and the body is more than clothing.

392
00:26:33,040 --> 00:26:41,140
So he addresses this wealthy landowner, younger son, and he says, look, dude, like, your issue is probably greed.

393
00:26:41,140 --> 00:26:43,780
Probably greed.

394
00:26:43,780 --> 00:26:47,300
I don't need to be the Son of God to tell you that you're greedy.

395
00:26:47,300 --> 00:26:53,080
And then he looks at his disciples, who I don't think greed is an issue for the disciples.

396
00:26:53,080 --> 00:26:59,180
They have given up pretty much everything they have to follow a, like, homeless, itinerant rabbi.

397
00:26:59,760 --> 00:27:06,780
But he looks to his disciples, and he pinpoints something that their view of money reveals about their heart, and that is anxiety.

398
00:27:06,780 --> 00:27:12,680
His disciples have sold most of what they have to follow a homeless, itinerant rabbi.

399
00:27:12,680 --> 00:27:16,080
Greed isn't likely their heart posture, but anxiety might be.

400
00:27:16,080 --> 00:27:22,260
And for many of us in the room, this is likely the primary emotion we feel when the topic of money comes up.

401
00:27:22,260 --> 00:27:26,700
The sermon bumper started rolling, and anxiety probably rose in the room for some of you.

402
00:27:26,760 --> 00:27:35,180
There is this scarcity illusion that has us anxious that we won't be able to keep up with our bills or provide for our kids what their peers have.

403
00:27:35,180 --> 00:27:38,400
We don't want to talk about or even think about money.

404
00:27:38,400 --> 00:27:40,320
We'd rather ignore the topic altogether.

405
00:27:43,280 --> 00:27:55,800
And the reality is that this scarcity illusion, I want to be contextual and understand here that this illusion that we're talking about, that Jesus is exposing, it is an illusion.

406
00:27:55,800 --> 00:27:59,460
But when enough people believe it, it becomes reality.

407
00:28:01,200 --> 00:28:09,860
And many people in the crowd and many people in the room are anxious for food and clothes because they work for people like the rich man in the parable.

408
00:28:09,860 --> 00:28:20,940
And the economy in the first century is not that much different than the economy here where it's hard to get rich, but once you're there, it's really easy to get richer.

409
00:28:20,940 --> 00:28:26,320
And it's really hard for those below them to get above where they're at.

410
00:28:26,320 --> 00:28:33,320
And many of us feel somewhat trapped in our economic class because our system makes it easier for the rich to get richer and the poor to stay where they are.

411
00:28:33,400 --> 00:28:39,260
So I don't want to act like that isn't a reality that might cause anxiety in many of our hearts.

412
00:28:39,260 --> 00:28:51,500
And in Luke, when Jesus first announces the kingdom of God, in Luke chapter 4, he gets baptized, he goes into the wilderness for the temptation.

413
00:28:51,500 --> 00:29:00,000
And his first declaration of what he came to preach, the kingdom of God, in Luke, he says that the kingdom of God is good news to the poor.

414
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:03,620
And the time of the Lord's favor has come.

415
00:29:03,620 --> 00:29:07,580
And so, yes, this is an illusion that has become a reality.

416
00:29:07,580 --> 00:29:14,560
But what Jesus is inviting us into is to reject the view of scarcity in the kingdom of under the sun.

417
00:29:14,560 --> 00:29:18,400
And he's inviting us to embrace the view of abundance in the kingdom of God.

418
00:29:18,700 --> 00:29:29,000
And the only way that the gospel becomes good news to the poor is that when those of us who have resources realize that we have more than we need and that we're invited to share with others,

419
00:29:29,000 --> 00:29:35,600
that's when we start to break the lie of the enemy, of the powers and principalities that have us kind of under the sun reality.

420
00:29:35,600 --> 00:29:37,940
We're locked in and we're lost in it.

421
00:29:37,940 --> 00:29:43,160
And we're invited to lay that lie down and to use our abundance to help those around us.

422
00:29:43,160 --> 00:29:45,860
That's when the kingdom of God becomes good news to the poor.

423
00:29:45,860 --> 00:29:46,540
Amen.

424
00:29:48,700 --> 00:29:56,360
And even though we really can't blame the anxious people about their anxiety, Jesus doesn't let them off the hook.

425
00:29:56,360 --> 00:29:57,940
He wants them also.

426
00:29:57,940 --> 00:30:05,280
He wants the greedy and the anxious to get their eyes above the sun, above this earthly kingdom reality to the kingdom of God.

427
00:30:05,280 --> 00:30:06,320
He tells this story.

428
00:30:06,320 --> 00:30:07,580
For life is more than food.

429
00:30:07,580 --> 00:30:08,860
The body is more than clothing.

430
00:30:08,860 --> 00:30:10,620
Consider the ravens.

431
00:30:10,620 --> 00:30:12,540
They neither sow nor reap.

432
00:30:13,660 --> 00:30:17,160
They have no storehouses or barns and yet God feeds them.

433
00:30:17,160 --> 00:30:19,960
How much more value are you than the birds?

434
00:30:19,960 --> 00:30:24,540
And which of you by being anxious can add a single hour to your lifespan?

435
00:30:24,540 --> 00:30:29,820
If then you are not able to do a small thing like that, why are you anxious about the rest?

436
00:30:29,820 --> 00:30:32,060
Consider the lilies, how they grow.

437
00:30:32,060 --> 00:30:33,640
They neither toil nor spin.

438
00:30:33,640 --> 00:30:38,600
Yet I tell you, even Solomon in all his glory was not arrayed like one of these.

439
00:30:39,400 --> 00:30:40,560
But it is God.

440
00:30:40,560 --> 00:30:49,100
But if God so clothes the grass which is alive in the field today and tomorrow is thrown in the oven, how much more will he clothe you, O you of little faith?

441
00:30:49,100 --> 00:30:53,840
Do not seek what you are to eat or what you are to drink, nor be worried.

442
00:30:53,840 --> 00:30:57,400
For all the nations of the world seek after these things.

443
00:30:57,400 --> 00:30:59,460
Your Father knows you need them.

444
00:30:59,520 --> 00:31:04,220
Instead, seek his kingdom and these things will be added to you.

445
00:31:04,220 --> 00:31:12,400
So Jesus kind of demonstrates, shares this illusion that we're all believing and holding on to, that there's limited resources and that life is short.

446
00:31:12,400 --> 00:31:19,780
And he's inviting us to see that there is a God who is a God of abundance, who provides for the birds of the air and the flowers of the ground.

447
00:31:19,780 --> 00:31:29,040
And if this is the God who created everything and who made you in his image, then there is not just abundance for the flowers and the birds, but there is an abundance for you.

448
00:31:29,040 --> 00:31:36,820
And we have to begin to lift our eyes above the worldly principalities and powers, the illusion of scarcity and temporary life.

449
00:31:36,820 --> 00:31:40,400
And we have to believe that we were created not just for life here now, but for eternity.

450
00:31:40,400 --> 00:31:45,080
And that there is more than enough because God is the God who made everything.

451
00:31:45,080 --> 00:31:50,420
This is the truest way of seeing God's world as it is in heaven.

452
00:31:50,420 --> 00:31:53,160
It confronts both the greedy rich and the anxious poor.

453
00:31:53,160 --> 00:31:55,140
None of us are off the hook in this conversation.

454
00:31:55,140 --> 00:32:01,000
And it ultimately isn't a conversation about money, but about the way we see the world and the way we relate to one another.

455
00:32:01,000 --> 00:32:05,700
Greed and worry are two ways of living inside the same illusion.

456
00:32:05,700 --> 00:32:09,840
And Jesus says, look at the birds and look at the flowers.

457
00:32:09,840 --> 00:32:10,700
They don't store food.

458
00:32:10,700 --> 00:32:12,120
They aren't anxious about what to wear.

459
00:32:12,120 --> 00:32:16,780
And yet their heavenly father clothes them and feeds them.

460
00:32:16,780 --> 00:32:23,720
Verse 30 and 31 just directly confronts this two kingdom mindset.

461
00:32:23,720 --> 00:32:27,740
He said, all the nations of the world, they all worry about where their food is going to come from.

462
00:32:27,740 --> 00:32:33,780
But you, if you have embraced the reality of the kingdom of God, you don't have to worry about these things.

463
00:32:33,780 --> 00:32:38,460
If you seek first his kingdom, all of these things will be added to you.

464
00:32:38,900 --> 00:32:46,020
And just to keep our theme from Ephesians and Genesis, I threw up a slide here that I think is really helpful to understand what Jesus is doing.

465
00:32:46,020 --> 00:32:47,060
I think, do I have it?

466
00:32:47,060 --> 00:32:48,280
There it is.

467
00:32:48,280 --> 00:32:49,480
I came to your side.

468
00:32:51,420 --> 00:32:52,320
Yes, I did it.

469
00:32:52,320 --> 00:32:58,600
We've been looking at these two realities of the world, the temporary reality of life under the sun.

470
00:32:58,600 --> 00:33:04,620
And it is animated by the sweat of the brow, the anxiety that there won't be enough and that I have to provide for me and mine.

471
00:33:04,620 --> 00:33:07,400
And that makes everybody that is not me and mine my enemy.

472
00:33:07,400 --> 00:33:13,980
And in competition for a limited amount of resources, it says that life is temporary, that resources are limited, and it leads to greed or fear.

473
00:33:14,140 --> 00:33:29,320
But thanks be to God for the cross, the empty tomb, the resurrection, and the ascension, inviting us into a new way of viewing reality that is good news for the poor, that life is not temporary but eternal, that resources are not limited but abundant.

474
00:33:29,520 --> 00:33:34,420
And that leads us to live with generous, open hands that lead to true and abundant life.

475
00:33:34,420 --> 00:33:38,900
This is what Jesus is trying to do here in this story.

476
00:33:38,900 --> 00:33:43,840
The old humanity, the kingdom of this world, believes the lie of the enemy.

477
00:33:43,840 --> 00:33:50,000
And we just grab more stuff and squeeze as much temporary enjoyment as we can out of our short lives.

478
00:33:50,000 --> 00:33:56,060
And the invitation from Jesus is to embrace the kingdom of heaven, here and now, to realize life is eternal.

479
00:33:56,380 --> 00:33:59,380
And in God's redeemed world, there is more than enough for everyone.

480
00:33:59,380 --> 00:34:07,100
We can begin to live towards this reality even before we see it fully because it leads to true and abundant life.

481
00:34:07,100 --> 00:34:16,420
My main point for this message this morning is that the illusion of scarcity produces greed and fear, and the abundance of God's kingdom produces generosity and joy.

482
00:34:16,420 --> 00:34:24,600
Peace and joy come from living with an open hands towards other, and you don't have to have a lot to start living into this kingdom.

483
00:34:25,340 --> 00:34:32,760
You don't even have to have financial resources to start being generous with your time and your energy and your prayers and your thoughts.

484
00:34:32,760 --> 00:34:35,420
You can begin to live with open hands.

485
00:34:35,420 --> 00:34:36,560
You don't have to be anxious.

486
00:34:36,560 --> 00:34:40,940
Even if you don't have everything, when we pray, God gave us this prayer.

487
00:34:40,940 --> 00:34:42,880
Give us this day our daily bread.

488
00:34:42,880 --> 00:34:47,260
He gave that prayer to people that literally didn't know where their meal was going to come from the next day.

489
00:34:48,420 --> 00:34:52,080
He's saying, trust me, pray to me, believe in me.

490
00:34:52,080 --> 00:34:55,300
We can live in this reality here and now.

491
00:34:55,300 --> 00:35:00,100
And then he lands the plane as Jesus often does with just a killer one-liner.

492
00:35:01,760 --> 00:35:10,800
He says, fear not, little flock, for it is your father's good pleasure to give you the kingdom.

493
00:35:10,800 --> 00:35:14,540
He says, don't be afraid.

494
00:35:14,540 --> 00:35:16,520
He refers to the crowd like sheep.

495
00:35:16,520 --> 00:35:25,920
They know this imagery well, that God is like a good shepherd who leads us beside still waters, who provides for our needs.

496
00:35:26,140 --> 00:35:38,120
It's an allusion in my mind to John chapter 10 where it says the thief, the enemy, the powers and principalities who are trying to convince you to believe that your life is short and that resources are limited.

497
00:35:38,120 --> 00:35:41,620
The purpose of the enemy is to steal, kill, and destroy.

498
00:35:41,620 --> 00:35:45,180
But Jesus says, I have come to give you life and life more abundantly.

499
00:35:45,180 --> 00:35:49,040
I am the good shepherd and the sheep hear my voice and they follow me.

500
00:35:49,040 --> 00:35:53,360
The question becomes, whose voice are we listening to?

501
00:35:53,360 --> 00:35:56,120
What view of reality are we believing?

502
00:35:56,120 --> 00:36:02,300
It is your father's good pleasure to give you the kingdom.

503
00:36:02,300 --> 00:36:14,380
And for those of us that grew up in the church, you might have kind of gotten a message that God's this angry God up in the sky who like is giving you stuff that he really doesn't want to give you.

504
00:36:14,380 --> 00:36:18,900
And that is not the biblical view of God at all.

505
00:36:19,140 --> 00:36:24,760
The biblical view of God is a God who is eager and excited.

506
00:36:26,140 --> 00:36:29,380
It is his good pleasure to give you the kingdom.

507
00:36:29,380 --> 00:36:30,500
You don't have to earn it.

508
00:36:30,500 --> 00:36:31,800
You don't have to strive for it.

509
00:36:31,800 --> 00:36:33,120
You don't have to store it up.

510
00:36:33,120 --> 00:36:37,340
It is a gift that is freely given.

511
00:36:37,340 --> 00:36:41,980
Our passage opened.

512
00:36:44,100 --> 00:36:52,460
I have to talk to you guys about the aha moments in sermon prep when you are like, sorry, I already got a little anxiety about preaching a message on money.

513
00:36:52,460 --> 00:36:56,640
Like I really want people to see Jesus clearly and beautifully in the midst of talking about money.

514
00:36:56,640 --> 00:36:57,860
Because again, we are not talking about money.

515
00:36:57,860 --> 00:36:59,740
We are talking about the heart.

516
00:37:01,040 --> 00:37:16,960
And I had this aha moment like Wednesday afternoon that the passage we read today, it starts with the younger brother asking a question triggered by the firstborn son selfishly hoarding the limited inheritance of his earthly father.

517
00:37:18,420 --> 00:37:30,220
And it ends with the one true firstborn son, sacrificially and generously distributing unlimited inheritance of an eternal father for all those who would receive it.

518
00:37:30,220 --> 00:37:35,340
We have these two kingdoms just put in juxtaposition with one another.

519
00:37:35,340 --> 00:37:43,960
The temporary earthly kingdom, the sons fighting over the resources, the older brother, the firstborn son keeping from his younger brother.

520
00:37:43,960 --> 00:38:00,000
And then we have the gospel, which is the one true firstborn son, that God sent his one and only son who would sacrificially lay down his life to distribute the abundance of an eternal God to those of us who would receive it by faith.

521
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:01,760
This is the gospel.

522
00:38:01,760 --> 00:38:03,860
This is God's grace.

523
00:38:03,860 --> 00:38:07,840
This leads to a view of the world from an abundance perspective.

524
00:38:07,840 --> 00:38:13,440
It invites us to live with open hands and it makes the gospel good news to the poor.

525
00:38:13,960 --> 00:38:16,760
But we have to see it.

526
00:38:16,760 --> 00:38:19,940
We have to believe it and we have to live into it.

527
00:38:19,940 --> 00:38:28,320
I think this is a beautiful vision that most of us can get excited about.

528
00:38:28,320 --> 00:38:32,860
But if we're honest, it hasn't fully trickled down to the way we handle our finances.

529
00:38:32,860 --> 00:38:39,460
We still put way too much trust in money and we're afraid of what living more generously will do to our security.

530
00:38:39,460 --> 00:38:43,540
Our head is in the kingdom, but our heart and our wallet is still under the sun.

531
00:38:43,960 --> 00:38:53,580
And the solution that Jesus offers is not a fun one, but it's Jesus, so it's good.

532
00:38:53,580 --> 00:38:55,920
He says, sell your possessions, give to the needy.

533
00:38:55,920 --> 00:39:01,380
Provide yourselves with money bags that do not grow old, with a treasure in heaven that does not fail,

534
00:39:01,380 --> 00:39:03,940
where no thief approaches and no moth destroys.

535
00:39:03,940 --> 00:39:07,180
For where your treasure is, there your heart will be also.

536
00:39:07,980 --> 00:39:14,560
Jesus says, if your head is in the kingdom and your heart is still under the sun, trust me and give it away.

537
00:39:14,560 --> 00:39:17,340
Try it and see what happens.

538
00:39:17,340 --> 00:39:21,880
He seems to be saying that you can actually move your heart by moving your money.

539
00:39:22,900 --> 00:39:29,540
Like if you want to have a life of open-handed abundance, generosity, and yet you're still clinging tight to it.

540
00:39:29,540 --> 00:39:34,240
He seems to say you can actually move your heart by moving your money.

541
00:39:34,240 --> 00:39:39,140
It will begin slowly over time to reshape the way you view reality.

542
00:39:39,140 --> 00:39:42,780
You will begin to see where true and abundant life is found.

543
00:39:44,080 --> 00:39:55,300
So if you're in here and you don't yet know Jesus, I just ask you, is it possible that you've been believing a lie about what life is really all about?

544
00:39:55,300 --> 00:40:03,740
Is it possible that life isn't actually just 60 to 80 years, 60 to 100 whatever years?

545
00:40:03,740 --> 00:40:10,540
Is it possible that the God who made all of creation has actually created you to live for eternity?

546
00:40:10,540 --> 00:40:13,480
And you can begin that process now.

547
00:40:13,540 --> 00:40:15,360
I just invite you to consider that reality.

548
00:40:15,360 --> 00:40:20,320
If that's something you want to talk to me about or somebody at the prayer team, we'd love to talk to you about that.

549
00:40:20,320 --> 00:40:25,980
For those of you that have a good handle on your finances, take a look at your saving, your spending, and your generosity.

550
00:40:25,980 --> 00:40:29,860
Ask yourself, what does this pattern reveal to me about where I'm putting my trust?

551
00:40:29,860 --> 00:40:34,300
If you're in here and you've got no clue what's going on with your money, that's okay.

552
00:40:34,300 --> 00:40:34,920
I've been there.

553
00:40:34,920 --> 00:40:35,500
Believe me.

554
00:40:35,500 --> 00:40:38,760
This is not a message of shame or guilt.

555
00:40:38,840 --> 00:40:43,860
It's an invitation to begin to open your heart to God.

556
00:40:43,860 --> 00:40:45,320
Be intentional.

557
00:40:45,320 --> 00:40:46,100
Make a plan.

558
00:40:46,100 --> 00:40:47,760
Work towards open-handed generosity.

559
00:40:47,760 --> 00:40:57,380
It might be 10 years before you can give $1 to somebody because you've got so much need and deficit between what you have and what you can give.

560
00:40:57,380 --> 00:40:58,660
That's okay.

561
00:40:59,660 --> 00:41:02,520
Jesus is inviting you to an eternal process.

562
00:41:02,520 --> 00:41:09,760
Jesus announces the kingdom of God.

563
00:41:09,840 --> 00:41:14,160
The spirit of the Lord is upon me for he has anointed me to bring good news to the poor.

564
00:41:14,160 --> 00:41:22,600
Just invite us to imagine a church that becomes a place that embodies this reality of God's kingdom to our community.

565
00:41:22,600 --> 00:41:34,820
That we wouldn't just be a church that says the gospel is good news to the poor, but we would be a church that lives with open hands and demonstrates to people who are in need that don't yet know Jesus.

566
00:41:36,500 --> 00:41:38,700
That this is a reality about his kingdom.

567
00:41:38,700 --> 00:41:46,440
Imagine a church where we don't just pray, give us this day our daily bread, but we look for opportunities to provide daily bread for those around us who are in need.

568
00:41:46,440 --> 00:41:55,360
My prayer for our church is that God would give us open eyes to see his kingdom more clearly and open hands to participate in his kingdom more freely.

569
00:41:55,360 --> 00:41:56,540
Let's pray.

570
00:41:56,540 --> 00:42:05,100
Father, we thank you.

571
00:42:06,500 --> 00:42:07,820
For the one true son.

572
00:42:07,820 --> 00:42:13,140
All of the inheritance is his.

573
00:42:13,140 --> 00:42:22,400
And yet he did not count his place of equality with God as something to be grasped, but he stooped down.

574
00:42:25,440 --> 00:42:37,220
Sacrificially laying down his life for you, for me, for us, so that we might freely inherit the abundance of God's kingdom.

575
00:42:37,220 --> 00:42:46,800
At the right time, you saw us and you were Jehovah Jireh, the provider of our every need.

576
00:42:48,920 --> 00:42:56,980
God, for those of us that are crippled with anxiety around our finances this morning, I pray that you would breathe on them peace.

577
00:42:58,380 --> 00:43:10,580
God, I pray that you would get their eyes above their bank accounts and that as they walk out of this place, they would see your abundance all around them.

578
00:43:10,580 --> 00:43:17,420
God, I pray that there would be people in their lives who know you or surrender to you that are prompted to meet their needs.

579
00:43:18,080 --> 00:43:33,900
God, for those of us who have more than enough, and we have eyes to see, ears to hear, and hands to participate in your kingdom being good news to those who don't have what they need.

580
00:43:33,900 --> 00:43:37,360
For your glory, for our good, and for the good of our neighbor.

581
00:43:37,360 --> 00:43:39,420
It's in Jesus' name I pray.

582
00:43:39,420 --> 00:43:40,460
Amen.

583
00:43:40,460 --> 00:43:40,540
Amen.

584
00:43:40,540 --> 00:43:40,600
Amen.
